Package: netsups
Version: __VERSION__
Architecture: __ARCH__
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: 疯狂的大叔 <HUiTHEME@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), systemd, python3 (>= 3.8), iputils-ping, polkitd
Description: Network UPS - power off this NAS when mains power is lost
 When several NAS units share a single UPS, only one of them receives the
 UPS power-loss signal. This app makes the other NAS units periodically ping
 a device powered from the same mains circuit. That device goes offline as
 soon as mains power is lost, which this app treats as a power failure and
 answers with a safe shutdown, protecting the hardware and disks from an
 abrupt outage.
 .
 Runs as a dedicated non-root user and only listens on a Unix socket behind
 the TOS API gateway, so it occupies no TCP port.
